  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">222878_Start Fund (Anticipation of food insecurity) Angola 822</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water Point Rehabilitation WVA will implement water point rehabilitation in the municipality of Chibia in Huila province. This is anticipatory action to mitigate the effects the drought and the fact that we have now entered in the dry season. Vulnerable and food insecure populations in Chibia will need access to potable water to avoid water borne diseases which could further lead to higher levels of malnutrition among children between 6 and 50 months in particular. In addition to access to water for humans, the rehabilitation will also allow cattle to gain access to water. 
 
 Training Water Committee members on water point maintenance and hygiene WVA will also identify together with the community and traditional leaders 8 members (per water point) who will comprise the Water Management Committee. While the water point is rehabilitation is done, the water management committee members will be trained in the management of the water point and in issue related to hygiene and sanitation.</narrative>
  </description>
